==================================== INPUT ====================================
//- src/Fragments.js

// A server-owned document cannot spread an `@inline` fragment that spreads a
// client fragment: the server reads the `@inline` data, so no client boundary
// would hand the client fragment's data off to the client.
graphql`fragment ServerParent_user on User @server {
  ...InlineCard_user
}`

graphql`fragment InlineCard_user on User @inline {
  name
  ...ClientCard_user @alias(as: "card")
}`

graphql`fragment ClientCard_user on User {
  picture
}`

//- relay.config.json
{
  "sources": {"src": "test_project"},
  "projects": {
    "test_project": {
      "schema": "schema.graphql",
      "language": "javascript",
      "featureFlags": {
        "enable_relay_rsc": true
      }
    }
  }
}

//- schema.graphql
type Query {
  me: User
}

type User {
  name: String
  picture: String
}
==================================== OUTPUT ===================================
✖︎ Server-owned document `ServerParent_user` cannot spread `@inline` fragment `InlineCard_user` because it spreads client fragment `ClientCard_user`: the server reads `@inline` data, so that client fragment's data would not be handed off to the client. Spread `ClientCard_user` with `@alias` directly in the server-owned document instead.

